msgstr "``application_id`` klient robí objav."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Domov Asistent prehľadá symbol na účet, ktorý razil. Toto rozmiestnenie je pre správcu, takže prichádza hovor ako správca, ktorý požiadal klienta. Expozícia subjektu stále hraničí dosah. Dostať sa k serveru nástrojov je na role as ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattters hraničí hovor na účet token patrí. Toto nasadenie mincovne, že osobný prístup token pre správcu účtu, takže hovory prísť s týmto účtom a práva, kto požiadal. Dosiahnutie servera nástrojov je na role ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: API Token je vydaný proti účtu správcu, takže každý hovor nesie, že účet a práva bez ohľadu na to, kto požiadal klienta. Dosiahnutie servera nástrojov je na role ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC, ktorá je samostatným grantom od správy Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: osobný prístup token je razený proti ``root`` účet a uložený pod ``administrator`` kľúč, takže každý hovor nesie tento účet má práva bez ohľadu na to, kto požiadal klienta. Dosiahnutie servera nástrojov je na role ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC, ktorá je samostatným grantom od správy GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: web-service token je vydaný proti správcovi účtu, takže hovor nesie tento účet a práva bez ohľadu na to, kto požiadal klienta. Pripojené funkcie sú iba na čítanie, čo hraničí s tým, čo môžu tieto práva robiť tu. Dosiahnutie servera nástrojov je na role ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Prichádza hovor. Baserow ako koncový vlastník bez ohľadu na to, kto požiadal klienta, a dosiahne iba jeden pracovný priestor, ktorý účet vlastní. To je druhá viazaná pod adaptérmi umožňuje zoznam, nie náhrada za neho."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC, ktorá je samostatným grantom od podniku Nextcloud účet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: identity MCP hovory vykonávať ako. ``user`` a ``oidc`` navyše vyžadujú ``delegation`` blok, pretože predaný nasadenie nositeľ je servisný účet bez ohľadu na to, čo metaúdaje tvrdí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` s tokenom z údajov o objave"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: autentifikačná schéma chrániaca koncový ukazovateľ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` je poradenstvo a nikdy zlyhá jednotka ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, takže skontrolujte, či hostiteľ očakávate, že snímka nie. A uvádza ``btrfs``/``zfs`` namiesto toho zlyhá jednotka, čo je bod jej uvedenia. Pred každou snímkou launcher tiež odstráni ``.baudolo-*`` Zabitý beh zanecháva vnútri data root."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: ``cloud`` alebo ``chezmoi``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (reťazec): základný adresár pre CA súbory"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans schéma v jednom Psql relácie a prehráva skládku v ďalšom, takže spotrebiteľ, ktorý topánky medzi znovu vytvorí schému a opakovaný záznam zomrie na vlastnú päsť ``CREATE TABLE``. Odmietnutie, zatiaľ čo spotrebiteľ je hore."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` používa centrálnu MariaDB ``root`` vytvoriť na mieste DB pri prvom nasadení."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` len niekedy existuje vnútri EspoCRM prostredníctvom automatického poskytovania OIDC (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas beží v každom variante."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` uvádza, ako pevne role páry k službe, ktorú vyhlasuje: ``>= 1`` drží partnera na tom istom hostiteľovi, ``< 1`` Nechá to žiť na vlastnú päsť. Hodnota sedí na strane spotrebiteľa vzťahu, takže dvojica je nasmerovaná a dva smery jedného páru nemusia súhlasiť."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **parent** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"
msgstr "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **materská** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ca_cert_host`` is where sys-ca-selfsigned provisions the root CA on the host. The container-side bind-mount targets live in the ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) and reach the standalone runtime scripts as env vars and CLI arguments."
msgstr "``ca_cert_host`` kde sys-ca-selfsigned poskytuje základné CA na hostiteľa. Záväzné ciele na strane kontajnera žijú v ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) a dosiahnuť samostatné runtime skripty ako env vars a CLI argumenty."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``canonical_domain`` is the host of ``canonical_url``, not the configured domain, so both follow the onion substitution a Tor deployment applies. A consumer that compares it against what a page actually renders would otherwise never match on an onion host."
msgstr "``canonical_domain`` je hostiteľom ``canonical_url``, nie nakonfigurovaná doména, takže obe nasledujú substitúciu cibule a tor nasadenie platí. Spotrebiteľ, ktorý ho porovnáva s tým, čo stránka skutočne robí, by sa inak nikdy nezhodoval s cibuľovým hostiteľom."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``central_mariadb_root_password``: The root password for the MariaDB server."
msgstr "``central_mariadb_root_password``: Root heslo pre MariaDB server."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``cert_host`` (string): host path to Root CA certificate"
msgstr "``cert_host`` (reťazec): host cesta k Root CA certifikátu"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``classification``:  what this role is in the MCP audit. Required."
msgstr "``classification``: aká je táto úloha v MCP audite. Vyžaduje sa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``comments`` is the parsed per-key comment map from default.env (see :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamic keys carry their comments via each handler's ``COMMENT`` constant. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (see :func:`apply_custom_env`)."
msgstr "``comments`` je spracovaný na-key komentár mapa od default.env (Pozri :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamické kľúče nesú svoje komentáre prostredníctvom každého správcu ``COMMENT`` konštantné. ``custom.env`` @ info: tooltip (Pozri :func:`apply_custom_env`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose build`` re-bakes the static output whenever the cloned content changes, so deploys are content-driven without any runtime build step."
msgstr "``compose build`` prebaľuje statický výstup vždy, keď sa zmení klonovaný obsah, takže nasadzuje sa obsahovo riadený bez akéhokoľvek kroku budovania času."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` and ``pip.conf.j2`` under ``templates/``, and the shell scripts under ``files/``, belong to the development compose stack, which drives them through `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ and `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. The Ansible deployment reads none of them."
msgstr "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` a ``pip.conf.j2`` pod ``templates/``, a skripty shell pod ``files/``, patrí do vývoja kompozitu, ktorý ich poháňa cez `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ a `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. Nasadenie Ansible nečíta nič z toho."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` (deprecated)"
msgstr "``compose`` (deprekovaný)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` is the in-repo Docker Compose stack. It remains installable but receives no new features."
msgstr "``compose`` je in-repo Docker Compose stack. Zostáva nainštalovateľný, ale neprijíma žiadne nové funkcie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` or ``swarm`` to pin every image to that track, ``rotate`` to split the images across both."
msgstr "``compose`` alebo ``swarm`` prišiť každý obrázok na tú trať, ``rotate`` rozdeliť obrázky na obe strany."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``composer install`` failed."
msgstr "``composer install`` zlyhal."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``config.access_grants: []``, administrator-only rather than public"
msgstr "``config.access_grants: []``, administrátorom a nie verejnosti"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer_not_allowed`` is a decision and simply narrows the result. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` and ``tools_unenforceable`` mean the provider did authorize this consumer and the connection still cannot be rendered, so they abort the run instead of disappearing quietly: a client that silently ends up with fewer tools than the deployment declared is indistinguishable from one that works."
msgstr "``consumer_not_allowed`` je rozhodnutie a jednoducho zužuje výsledok. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` a ``tools_unenforceable`` znamená, že poskytovateľ povolil tohto spotrebiteľa a pripojenie stále nemôže byť vykonané, takže prerušia beh namiesto zmiznutia potichu: klient, ktorý ticho končí s menej nástrojov, než je deklarované nasadenie je nerozoznateľný od toho, ktorý funguje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer``: optional override"
msgstr "``consumer``: voliteľné preradenie"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``container system prune -a -f`` to remove unused Docker resources."
msgstr "``container system prune -a -f`` odstrániť nevyužité zdroje Docker."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``core`` for every language but the source language, ``docs`` for the languages LibreTranslate supports."
msgstr "``core`` pre každý jazyk okrem zdrojového jazyka, ``docs`` pre jazyky LibreTranslate podpora."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential_missing`` is the one authorized rejection that does not abort, because a provider deploying later in the same play has not written its secret yet. That exemption ends at the reconciliation stage, which runs once every provider has: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` treats it as fatal there."
msgstr "``credential_missing`` je autorizované odmietnutie, ktoré nepozastavuje, pretože poskytovateľ, ktorý nasadzuje neskôr v rovnakej hre, ešte nenapísal svoje tajomstvo. Táto výnimka sa končí vo fáze zosúlaďovania, ktorá funguje po tom, ako každý poskytovateľ: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` Je to smrteľné."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential``:      which principal the provider authenticates as, and where its secret is read from. Replaces the administrator token path."
msgstr "``credential``: ktorý hlavný poskytovateľ autentifikuje ako, a kde je jeho tajomstvo prečítané. Nahradí cestu tokenu správcu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, sent as ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"
msgstr "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, odoslaná ako ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``custom.env`` is the operator's untracked override file; its values win over static defaults AND handler-computed values."
msgstr "``custom.env`` je nesledovaný súbor operátora s prepisom; jeho hodnoty vyhrajú nad statickými predvolenými hodnotami a hodnotami komanditnými."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_name``: The name of the initial database to create."
msgstr "``database_name``: Názov pôvodnej databázy vytvoriť."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_password``: The password for the database user."
msgstr "``database_password``: Heslo pre užívateľa databázy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_username``: The username for the database user."
msgstr "``database_username``: Užívateľské meno pre užívateľa databázy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``days`` (int): certificate validity"
msgstr "``days`` (int): platnosť certifikátu"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``default-address-pools`` is where docker takes that address from, so the declaration answers before the daemon exists and answers identically afterwards. That also keeps daemon.json byte-identical across passes, which the fact-derived value could not: it appeared only from the second run on and restarted the container runtime under a live stack."
msgstr "``default-address-pools`` je miesto, kde Docker preberá túto adresu, takže vyhlásenie odpovede pred démonom existuje a odpovede identické potom. To je tiež daemon.json bajte-identické prechody, ktoré fakt-odvodená hodnota nemohla: sa objavila len od druhého behu na a reštartoval kontajner beží pod živým zásobníkom."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``delegation``:      recorded proof, at one exact upstream version, that per-user token acquisition, refresh, audience binding and revocation exist."
msgstr "``delegation``: zaznamenal dôkaz, v jednej presnej verzii proti prúdu, že na-user token akvizície, obnoviť, publikum záväzné a zrušenie existujú."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``deployment`` restricts to roles present anywhere in ``groups``, which is what a container-network consumer can actually reach; ``all`` returns every declaring role, deployed or not."
msgstr "``deployment`` obmedzuje sa na úlohy prítomné kdekoľvek v ``groups``, čo je to, čo môže spotrebiteľ kontajnerovej siete skutočne dosiahnuť; ``all`` vracia každú deklaračnú úlohu, alebo nie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dest``: destination path (required for ``cloud``)"
msgstr "``dest``: cieľová trasa (požadované pre ``cloud``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``direction``:       whether the role exposes MCP, consumes it, or both."
msgstr "``direction``: či úloha odhaľuje MCP, spotrebuje, alebo oboje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``discourse``: the WP->Discourse post round-trip scenario. Disabling Discourse skips it; front-page reachability and CSP baselines stay active."
msgstr "``discourse``: WP->Discourse scenár po kole-trip. Zastavenie Discourse preskočí ju; prístupnosť na prvej strane a CSP základné hodnoty zostanú aktívne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``docker_name``    the explicit ``name:`` field (alias for ``name``"
msgstr "``docker_name`` explicitné ``name:`` pole (alias pre ``name``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``domains``: canonical and alias domains"
msgstr "``domains``: kanonické a prezývky"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``): run ``doli pull`` after adding mappings"
msgstr "``dotlinker_apply`` (predvolené: ``true``): beh ``doli pull`` po pridaní máp"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (predvolené: ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_config_path`` (predvolené: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_package_name`` (predvolené: ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): pass ``--replace`` to ``doli add``"
msgstr "``dotlinker_replace`` (predvolené: ``true``): prejsť ``--replace`` do ``doli add``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_user`` (required): user to run ``doli`` as"
msgstr "``dotlinker_user`` (požadované): užívateľ spustiť ``doli`` ako"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` and ``dsk-gnt-pi`` carry no entry in that map. Cursor is a full editor rather than an extension, and neither vendor publishes an extension on Open VSX, so there is nothing to install into Code for them. Both agents are used from their own binary."
msgstr "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` a ``dsk-gnt-pi`` na mape nie je žiadny záznam. Kurzor je úplný editor, nie rozšírenie, a ani jeden predajca publikuje rozšírenie na Open VSX, takže nie je čo inštalovať do Code pre nich. Obaja agenti sa používajú z vlastného binárneho."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enabled`` (bool)"
msgstr "``enabled`` (bool)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``endpoint``:        connection metadata for clients (server roles only)."
msgstr "``endpoint``: prístupové metaúdaje pre klientov (len úlohy servera)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enforced`` onions every capable row, ``disabled`` none, ``exclusive`` drops the rows that cannot take one, ``auto`` rotates."
msgstr "``enforced`` cibuľa každý schopný riadok, ``disabled`` žiadne, ``exclusive`` drops riadky, ktoré nemôžu vziať jeden, ``auto`` sa otáča."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries_only=true`` returns those strings as a list instead of the rendered block, for a container that is not described by a compose file at all: ``web-app-discourse`` is built by discourse_docker's ``launcher``, whose only argument surface is ``docker_args:`` in its ``app.yml``, so it needs ``--add-host=<entry>`` lines."
msgstr "``entries_only=true`` Description ``web-app-discourse`` je vybudovaná discourse_docker's ``launcher``, ktorého jediným argumentom je ``docker_args:`` v ``app.yml``, tak to potrebuje ``--add-host=<entry>`` riadky."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries`` is a list of dotted-path facts about the file's content. Each entry carries the same ``mandatory`` and ``allowed`` semantics described above and adds a ``marker`` flag (default ``False``): ``marker: True`` declares the path as the type marker for the surrounding type entry. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` walks every ``marker: True`` entry; each marker that resolves to a non-empty value in the role's file adds the surrounding type to the role's type set. ``application_id`` for ``application`` and ``system_service_id`` for ``system-service`` are the canonical markers."
msgstr "``entries`` je zoznam faktov o obsahu súboru. Každý záznam nesie rovnaký ``mandatory`` a ``allowed`` sémantika opísaná vyššie a pridáva ``marker`` vlajka (štandardná ``False``): ``marker: True`` vyhlasuje trasu ako značku typu pre vstup okolitého typu. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` Chodí každý ``marker: True`` vstup; každý markér, ktorý rieši neprázdnu hodnotu v súbore role pridáva okolitý typ do súboru typov role. ``application_id`` namiesto ``application`` a ``system_service_id`` namiesto ``system-service`` sú kanonické znaky."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declares a ``run-name:`` that interpolates the dispatch inputs. Once a run has started, that title is the only record of them: the REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch run. Anything that wants to know what a run was dispatched with therefore parses the title — and parsing it against a hand-copied format would drift the moment the workflow changes, silently and without a failing test."
msgstr "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` deklaruje a ``run-name:`` že interpoluje odosielacie vstupy. Akonáhle sa začne beh, tento názov je ich jediným záznamom: REST API odpovede ``inputs: null`` pre workflow_dispatch Bež. Čokoľvek, čo chce vedieť, čo beh bol odoslaný s preto parses titul."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ephemeral`` publishes the container port on a host port docker picks, for a service addressed only through the compose network."
msgstr "``ephemeral`` uverejní kontajnerový port na hostiteľskom porte docker tips, za službu adresovanú len prostredníctvom kompozície siete."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposed`` is an explicit per-service opt-in (default false) that makes the service reachable over the node onion: its port gets a dedicated ``HiddenServicePort``. Because ``applications`` is the variant-merged config (base ``meta/services.yml`` deep-merged with the round's ``meta/variants.yml`` override), a service is forwarded only in the variant/config where it sets ``exposed: true`` — which is exactly what lets the two DB variants be tested over Tor (v0 exposed -> reachable, v1 not -> refused)."
msgstr "``exposed`` je explicitný opt-in na službu (štandardná chyba) ktorý robí službu dosiahnuteľnú cez uzol cibule: jeho port dostane vyhradené ``HiddenServicePort``. Pretože. ``applications`` je fúzia s variantom (základ ``meta/services.yml`` Hlboko s guľometmi ``meta/variants.yml`` prepísať), služba sa zasiela iba v variante / config, kde sa stanovuje ``exposed: true`` Čo je presne to, čo umožňuje dva DB varianty byť testované cez Tor (v0 vystavené - > dosiahnuteľné, v1 nie -> odmietnuté)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposure``:        who may reach the endpoint."
msgstr "``exposure``: kto môže dosiahnuť koncový ukazovateľ."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``extra_hosts=``, whatever the call site needs on top: a peer's overlay VIP, or a partner service reachable only on the host."
msgstr "``extra_hosts=``, bez ohľadu na to, čo call stránky potrebujú navrchu: peer's prekrytie VIP, alebo partnerská služba dosiahnuteľná len na hostiteľa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``false`` while MCP servers are discovered"
msgstr "``false`` zatiaľ čo MCP servery sú objavené"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``family`` is the ``os_family`` ansible reports for the host. Callers that have facts (the action plugin) pass it, so distributions outside the CI matrix - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - still resolve through their family. Callers without facts (lints, the availability test) omit it and the family is derived from :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, which only covers the default matrix."
msgstr "``family`` je ``os_family`` ohromujúce správy pre hostiteľa. Volajúci, ktorí majú fakty (Akčný modul) prejsť, takže distribúcie mimo CI matice - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - stále vyriešiť prostredníctvom svojej rodiny. Volajúci bez faktov (Lints, test dostupnosti) vynechať a rodina je odvodená z :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, ktorá pokrýva iba štandardnú matricu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the filer web UI behind an admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` Slúži web UI súborov za admin-iba oauth2-proxy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (run on the deploy host) completes the first-run wizard (seeds the break-glass admin), installs both plugins via Jellyfin’s own ``/Packages`` installer, writes the plugin configs, and restarts."
msgstr "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (bežať na nasadenie hostiteľa) dokončí prvý-run sprievodca (semená admin lámacie sklo), inštaluje oba moduly cez JellyfinVlastné ``/Packages`` inštalátor, píše plugin konfiguruje, a reštartuje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/playwright.config.js``: shared Playwright configuration"
msgstr "``files/playwright.config.js``: spoločná konfigurácia Playwright"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/python/policy.py`` validates it at startup. A contract missing a limit, carrying an empty allowlist, naming a wildcard path or lacking a pinned schema hash is refused before the process serves anything."
msgstr "``files/python/policy.py`` Potvrdí to pri štarte. Zmluva, ktorej chýba limit, nesie prázdny zoznam povolení, pomenuje cestu po wildcard alebo chýba pripnutá schéma hašiš, je odmietnutá predtým, než proces slúži čokoľvek."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flags``: list of flags to AND. Default: ``[enabled, shared]``"
msgstr "``flags``: zoznam vlajok do A. Štandardné: ``[enabled, shared]``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flavor`` picks the probe shape (see utils/docker/healthcheck/); each flavor brings its own interval, timeout, retries and start_period, and any of those may be overridden next to it. Without a ``flavor`` the entry must carry an explicit ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` selects another entry below ``ports.internal`` for services that expose their probe on a second port."
msgstr "``flavor`` vyberá tvar sondy (Pozri utils/docker/healthcheck/); každá chuť prináša svoj vlastný interval, timeout, stravovanie a start_period, a niektoré z nich môže byť prekročená vedľa neho. Bez ``flavor`` zápis musí byť výslovný ``test`` Argv. ``port_key`` vyberie iný záznam nižšie ``ports.internal`` pre služby, ktoré odhaľujú ich sondu na druhom porte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``force_regen`` (bool): if true, remove and regenerate key/cert"
msgstr "``force_regen`` (bool): ak je to pravda, odstráňte a regenerujte kľúč/cert"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``forward[A]`` is the list of provider roles that ``A`` directly depends on (services it embeds). ``reverse[B]`` is the list of roles that directly depend on ``B`` (consumers that embed ``B``)."
msgstr "``forward[A]`` je zoznam úloh poskytovateľa, ktoré ``A`` priamo závisí od (služby, ktoré vloží). ``reverse[B]`` je zoznam úloh, ktoré priamo závisia od ``B`` (spotrebitelia, ktorí vložili ``B``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``galaxy_info.author`` is where a role records who implemented it, so that is where the names are read. A role may credit more than one person, comma separated."
msgstr "``galaxy_info.author`` je miesto, kde sú záznamy o úlohe, ktorí ju zaviedli, takže tam sa čítajú mená. Úloha môže pripísať viac ako jednu osobu, čiarka oddelené."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``getent`` honours nsswitch and cannot address a server, so on its own it cannot say which of the resolvers in resolv.conf refused. Where the distro ships a query tool, ask every nameserver directly; where it does not, the per-name verdicts still stand on their own."
msgstr "``getent`` pocty nswitch a nemôže adresovať server, takže sám o sebe nemôže povedať, ktorý z riešiteľov v resolv.conf odmietol. Tam, kde distro loďou dotaz nástroj, spýtajte sa každého menaserver priamo; kde to nie je, per-name verdikty stále stojí na ich vlastné."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` is the single source of truth for host paths. The env layer (utils/env/handlers, exported by scripts/meta/env/load.sh) derives the ``INFINITO_*`` env keys from it; a set env wins so callers can override. When a tool runs outside that layer, e.g. a bare ``subprocess`` that does not inherit the env build, the value is read straight from the group_vars SPOT, so there is still no hardcoded literal default."
msgstr "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` je jediným zdrojom pravdy pre hostiteľské cesty. Env vrstva (utils/env/handlers, vyvezené scripts/meta/env/load.sh) odvodzuje ``INFINITO_*`` Zásielkové kľúče z neho; set env vyhráva, takže volajúci môžu prepísať. Keď nástroj beží mimo tejto vrstvy, napr. holé ``subprocess`` ktorý nezdedí závisť vybudovať, hodnota je čítaná priamo z group_vars SPOT, takže stále nie je žiadny pevný kódovaný doslovný predvolený."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``host_alias=true``, which pins ``host.docker.internal`` at whatever reaches the host in the effective mode. A container that must talk to a service the host publishes -- msmtp relaying through the swarm ingress on :587, for instance -- needs the alias, and it must not hardcode ``host-gateway`` because that breaks under swarm for the reason below."
msgstr "``host_alias=true``, ktoré kolíky ``host.docker.internal`` na čokoľvek dosiahne hostiteľa v efektívnom režime. Kontajner, ktorý sa musí porozprávať so službou, ktorú hostiteľ publikuje -- smtp sa šíri cez rojný vchod na:587, napríklad -- potrebuje prezývku, a nesmie hardcode ``host-gateway`` Pretože sa to rozbije pod rojom z dôvodu nižšie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, own network only"
msgstr "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, len vlastná sieť"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` on the shared MCP overlay"
msgstr "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` o spoločnom prekrývaní MCP"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``implementation``:  how the surface is provided, ordered by precedence."
msgstr "``implementation``: ako je povrch k dispozícii, poradie podľa poradia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``in_container`` exists because one template serves two consumers. The host's /root/.msmtprc is read by the host and loopback is right for it; the copy mounted at /etc/msmtprc is read inside a container, where 127.0.0.1 is that container's own loopback and nothing listens on it. Such a service must also emit ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` so the alias resolves."
msgstr "``in_container`` existuje, pretože jedna šablóna slúži dvom spotrebiteľom. Hostiteľ /root/.msmtprc je prečítaný hostiteľom a sluckback je pre neho ten pravý; kópia pripojená na /etc/msmtprc sa číta vo vnútri kontajnera, kde 127.0.0.1 je to, že kontajner je vlastný spätný chod a nič ho nepočúva. Takáto služba musí tiež vysielať ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` Takže alias sa rozhodne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``indent=0`` collapses everything to the left edge - useful when the lookup is rendered into top-level YAML (no service wrapper)."
msgstr "``indent=0`` zrúti všetko na ľavej strane - užitočné, keď je vyhľadávanie prevedená do najvyššej úrovne YAML (žiadny servisný obal)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ingress`` (default) emits the short ``\"host:published:container\"`` string; ``host`` emits the long block with ``mode: host``, which is what an edge role needs in swarm so the client address survives the hop."
msgstr "``ingress`` (štandardná) emituje krátke ``\"host:published:container\"`` reťazec; ``host`` emituje dlhý blok s ``mode: host``, čo je to, čo hrana úloha potrebuje v roji tak klientská adresa prežije hop."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal`` (default) reads ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reuses the published port, for services that cannot remap (STUN/TURN, media relays)."
msgstr "``internal`` (štandardná) má byť ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` opakované použitie uverejneného prístavu v prípade služieb, ktoré nemôžu prepracovať (STUN/TURN, prenosy médií)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal``, container network only"
msgstr "``internal``, len sieť kontajnerov"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``kas`` (Kubernetes agent server, workspaces), ``pages``, ``registry`` and ``mailroom`` are not deployed; ``gitlab.yml`` disables them."
msgstr "``kas`` (Server agenta Kubernetes, pracovné priestory), ``pages``, ``registry`` a ``mailroom`` sa nepoužívajú; ``gitlab.yml`` zneškodní ich."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_bits`` (int): RSA key size"
msgstr "``key_bits`` (int): RSA veľkosť kľúča"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_host`` (string): host path to Root CA private key"
msgstr "``key_host`` (reťazec): host cesta k Root CA súkromný kľúč"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key`` names the pinned key and defaults to ``version``; an entity with several pins declares a list of such blocks. The types are ``git_tags`` (repository), ``registry_tags`` (image), ``npm`` (package), ``http_regex`` (url, pattern) and ``script`` (path, run with the current version and printing the latest one)."
msgstr "``key`` names the pinned key and defaults to ``version``; jednotka s niekoľkými kolíkmi vyhlasuje zoznam takýchto blokov. Typy sú ``git_tags`` (úložisko), ``registry_tags`` (obrázok), ``npm`` (balenie), ``http_regex`` (url, vzor) a ``script`` (cesta, beh s aktuálnou verziou a tlač najnovšej)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key``: services.<key>.* lookup base. Default: provides or entity_name"
msgstr "``key``: služby.<key>.* Pozrite sa na základňu. Štandardné: poskytuje alebo entity_name"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (default) | ``database`` | ``mcp_client`` | ``web_facing`` | ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` admits a role only when its ``mcp.direction`` is ``client`` or ``both`` AND it declares ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` without the provider refusing it through ``mcp_consumer: false`` on that same entry, so a provider's network carries the clients it admitted rather than every client in the deployment. Being a client is not an admission: without the second condition one admission anywhere reaches every provider that opens its overlay."
msgstr "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (štandardná) ``database`` ``mcp_client`` ``web_facing`` ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` pripúšťa úlohu len vtedy, keď ``mcp.direction`` ci ``client`` alebo ``both`` A vyhlasuje ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` bez toho, aby poskytovateľ odmietol ``mcp_consumer: false`` pri tom istom vstupe, takže sieť poskytovateľa nesie klientov, ktorých pripúšťa, a nie každého klienta pri nasadení. Byť klientom nie je vstup: bez druhej podmienky jeden vstup kdekoľvek osloví každého poskytovateľa, ktorý otvorí svoje krytie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``last`` seeds the OCI pagination cursor: only tags sorting lexically after it are returned. Repos like GitLab CNG carry tens of thousands of commit-sha tags before the ``v*`` release tags, so an unseeded scan exhausts ``max_pages`` without ever reaching them."
msgstr "``last`` semien kurzor paginácie OCI: iba značky triedenia lexicky po ich vrátení. Repo obchody podobné GitLab CNG má desaťtisíce značiek commit-sha pred ``v*`` uvoľňovanie štítkov, takže nenaštartované skenovanie výfukových plynov ``max_pages`` bez toho, aby som sa k nim dostal."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``latest`` is the last commit of the default branch. It is built at start and rebuilt whenever a fetch finds a new commit; the previous build stays online until the new one replaces it."
msgstr "``latest`` je posledný záväzok štandardnej pobočky. Je postavený na začiatku a prestavaný vždy, keď prilákanie nájde nový záväzok; predchádzajúca stavba zostáva online, kým ju nový nenahradí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``laya``, ``torch`` or ``onnx``; the role refuses anything else"
msgstr "``laya``, ``torch`` alebo ``onnx``; úloha odmieta čokoľvek iné"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ldap``: the three RBAC scenarios additionally depend on LDAP group sync; disabling LDAP skips them alongside OIDC."
msgstr "``ldap``: tri RBAC scenáre navyše závisí na LDAP skupiny synchronizácia; znemožňuje LDAP preskočí je vedľa OIDC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ldapauth`` is the only path that materialises a ``friendica.user`` row, so its enablement derives directly from the ``ldap`` service flag. The oauth2-proxy ``sso`` gate in front of the vhost is a front-door auth gate, not an addon bridge, and stays in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. The LDAP login path is covered by the existing LDAP Playwright spec (requirement 018), so no addon-specific spec is added."
msgstr "``ldapauth`` je jediná cesta, ktorá naplní ``friendica.user`` riadok, takže jeho možnosť pochádza priamo z ``ldap`` servisná vlajka. Oauth2-proxy ``sso`` Brána pred vhost je predo dvermi auth brána, nie addon most, a zostane v ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>` . Prihlasovacia cesta LDAP je pokrytá existujúcou špecifikáciou LDAP Playwright (požiadavka 018), takže nie je pridaná žiadna špecifická doplnková špecifikácia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``libaacs`` (AACS decryption library)"
msgstr "``libaacs`` (Dešifrovacia knižnica AACS)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``libbluray`` (Blu-ray playback support library)"
msgstr "``libbluray`` (Name)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lifecycle``  — maturity marker filtered by ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."
msgstr "``lifecycle`` ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``limits``:          the request, response, timeout, concurrency, pagination and stream ceilings the surface enforces."
msgstr "``limits``: žiadosť, odpoveď, timeout, concurrency, pagination a potok stropy povrch presadzuje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale-gen`` only re-runs when the template changes"
msgstr "``locale-gen`` len opätovné spustenie, keď sa zmení vzor"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale.conf``: sets ``LANG`` and ``LANGUAGE`` environment variables"
msgstr "``locale.conf``: sady ``LANG`` a ``LANGUAGE`` environmentálne premenné"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale.gen``: uncomment or specify the locales you need"
msgstr "``locale.gen``: odposluch alebo zadať miestne potrebujete"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('guide_role', application_id)`` picks the first invokable app the round deployed beside ``application_id``. Invokability comes from :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, so no caller re-derives it from role-name prefixes."
msgstr "``lookup('guide_role', application_id)`` vyberie prvú invokovateľnú aplikáciu v kole nasadenom vedľa ``application_id``. Invokovateľnosť pochádza z :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, takže žiadny volajúci znovu-podmieňuje to z predpony role-name."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('users', user_key).authorized_keys`` (list; may be empty)"
msgstr "``lookup('users', user_key).authorized_keys`` (zoznam; môže byť prázdny)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('users', user_key).username`` (defaults to ``user_key``)"
msgstr "``lookup('users', user_key).username`` (štandardné ``user_key``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``lookup('volume', application_id)`` — return the WHOLE canonical registry as a dict keyed by semantic name. Useful for tasks that loop over every declared volume (e.g. NFS subdir pre-creation). Returns ``{}`` for roles with no meta/volumes.yml."
msgstr "``lookup('volume', application_id)`` Užitočné pre úlohy, ktoré obiehajú nad každým deklarovaným objemom (napr. predprodukcia NFS subdir). Description ``{}`` pre úlohy bez meta/volumes.yml."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('volume', application_id, name)`` — return the normalised dict for a single semantic entry. The returned dict always carries:"
msgstr "``lookup('volume', application_id, name)`` Vrátený zákon vždy nesie:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``main.yml``: The main task file that handles the installation of GnuCash."
msgstr "``main.yml``: Hlavná úloha súbor, ktorý spracováva inštaláciu GnuCash."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``main`` unless ``repo_root`` is a linked git worktree, whose branch is lowercased and every character outside ``[a-z0-9_-]`` replaced by ``-``; ``None`` when the worktree's git directory is not reachable, as inside a container that mounts only the checkout."
msgstr "``main`` pokiaľ ``repo_root`` je prepojený git worktree, ktorého vetva je menšia a každý znak vonku ``[a-z0-9_-]`` nahradený ``-``; ``None`` keď adresár git worktree nie je dosiahnuteľný, ako vo vnútri kontajnera, ktorý pripojí len checkout."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``make install-lint`` used to ask GitHub for each tool’s latest tag at install time. That made every installation depend on the network resolving ``api.github.com``, and it silently changed the linter version between two runs of the same commit. Pinning moves the version into the repository, where it is reviewable and reproducible."
msgstr "``make install-lint`` sa spýtal GitHub pre každý nástroj a najnovšie značky v čase inštalácie. To spôsobilo, že každá inštalácia závisí od riešenia siete. ``api.github.com``, a to ticho zmenilo linter verziu medzi dvoma behmi rovnakého záväzku. Pinning presúva verziu do úložiska, kde je hodnotiteľná a reprodukovateľná."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``make install`` completed on the control machine (installs Ansible and Python dependencies)."
msgstr "``make install`` dokončené na ovládacom stroji (inštaluje Ansible a Python závislosti)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mandatory`` (default ``False``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MUST be present and non-empty for a role of this type. Implies ``allowed: True``; setting ``mandatory: True`` together with ``allowed: False`` is a schema error."
msgstr "``mandatory`` (štandardná ``False``): súbor (alebo bodkovaná cesta) MUSÍ byť prítomný a neprázdny pre úlohu tohto typu. Implementácie ``allowed: True``; nastavenie ``mandatory: True`` spolu s ``allowed: False`` je chyba schémy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``master.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the master web UI behind the same admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``master.seaweedfs.s3.*`` Slúži majstra webu UI za rovnakým admin-iba oauth2-proxy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``match`` keeps only the versions carrying that prefix, and ``strip`` removes it again, so a pin without the upstream's ``v`` stays without it."
msgstr "``match`` uchováva iba verzie s predponou a ``strip`` Odstráni to znova, takže špendlík bez protiprúdov ``v`` zostane bez nej."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mcp-server`` pinned to ``0.190.ve5a_6581ffc96`` in ```files/plugins.txt`` <./files/plugins.txt>`__"
msgstr "``mcp-server`` pripnuté na ``0.190.ve5a_6581ffc96`` on ```files/plugins.txt`` <./files/plugins.txt>`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mcp.enabled`` resolves to ``true`` only when ``web-app-hermes``, ``web-app-openclaw`` or ``web-app-openwebui`` is part of the same deployment, and is ``false`` otherwise. While it is ``true`` the deploy:"
msgstr "``mcp.enabled`` rozhodnutie ``true`` iba ak ``web-app-hermes``, ``web-app-openclaw`` alebo ``web-app-openwebui`` je súčasťou rovnakého nasadenia a je ``false`` inak. Kým to je ``true`` rozmiestnenie:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mcp`` declares the Model Context Protocol surface GitLab serves natively from its Rails API."
msgstr "``mcp`` deklaruje povrch vzorového kontextového protokolu GitLab slúži z pôvodných koľají API."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/addons/`` is also the download list: ``MEDIAWIKI_EXT_NAMES`` keeps only the addons whose ``enabled`` resolves true, so a deployment without the matching service never pulls that tarball or runs composer for it."
msgstr "``meta/addons/`` je tiež zoznam na stiahnutie: ``MEDIAWIKI_EXT_NAMES`` drží len doplnky, ktorých ``enabled`` rieši pravdu, takže nasadenie bez zodpovedajúce služby nikdy ťahá tarball alebo beží skladateľ pre neho."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/categories.yml`` at the repository root declares the nested category tree every role name is derived from: the dash-joined path of a node is the role's category prefix (``web`` -> ``app`` yields ``web-app-*``), and nodes carry the ``invokable``, ``stage``, ``modes`` and ``run_after`` policy the dispatcher, the stage lookup and the inventory generator read."
msgstr "``meta/categories.yml`` pri koreňovom úložisku deklaruje vnorený strom kategórie každý názov role je odvodený z: pomlčka-pripojený cesta uzla je predpona kategórie role (``web`` - > ``app`` výnosy ``web-app-*``), a uzly nesú ``invokable``, ``stage``, ``modes`` a ``run_after`` politiku dispečer, pódium vyhľadávanie a generátor zásob čítať."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/categories.yml`` declares the ordered ``stages`` (constructor -> workstation -> server -> destructor, matching ``tasks/stages/0*.yml``) and a ``stage`` per top-level category. This module resolves a role to its stage and exposes the canonical stage order, so both the CLI (``cli.meta.roles.order``) and the ``stage_order`` / ``role_stage`` lookups read one source of truth."
msgstr "``meta/categories.yml`` deklaruje príkaz ``stages`` (Konštruktor -> pracovná stanica -> server -> deštruktor, zodpovedajúce ``tasks/stages/0*.yml``) a ``stage`` v kategórii najvyššej úrovne. Tento modul rieši úlohu svojho štádia a odhaľuje poradie kanonického javiska, takže ako CLI (``cli.meta.roles.order``) a ``stage_order`` / ``role_stage`` Pohľady čítajú jeden zdroj pravdy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/distros.yml`` declares every distribution the project builds, tests and deploys on: the id used as ``INFINITO_DISTRO``, the ``os_family`` ansible reports for it, the Galaxy platform name, the upstream base image the development-environment matrix boots it from, and the templates the pkgmgr base image and the environment image references are rendered from."
msgstr "``meta/distros.yml`` deklaruje každú distribúciu projekt buduje, testuje a rozmiestňuje na: ID použitý ako ``INFINITO_DISTRO``, ``os_family`` Ansibble reports for it, the Galaxy platform name, the background base image the development-environment matrice boots it from, and the šablóns the pkgmgr base image and the environment image referencies are maturity from."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``meta/variants.yml`` defines three variants (mirrors the ``web-app-kix`` / ``web-app-zammad`` pattern):"
msgstr "``meta/variants.yml`` definuje tri varianty (odráža ``web-app-kix`` / ``web-app-zammad`` vzorka):"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mode`` selects placement semantics:"
msgstr "``mode`` vyberá umiestnenie sémantika:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``modes`` in ``meta/services.yml`` states where a role RUNS; ``skip`` in ``meta/tests.yml`` deactivates TESTING a mode without touching that capability."
msgstr "``modes`` on ``meta/services.yml`` uvádza úlohu RUNS; ``skip`` on ``meta/tests.yml`` deaktivuje skúšku režimu bez toho, aby sa dotkla tejto schopnosti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``modes``: list of DEPLOYMENT_MODE values where this overlay applies"
msgstr "``modes``: zoznam DEPLOYMENT_MODE hodnoty, pri ktorých sa uplatňuje toto prekrývanie"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mounts``         the raw mounts list, ``[]`` if absent"
msgstr "``mounts`` zoznam surových montážnych zariadení, ``[]`` ak chýba"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``msgctxt`` prefixes of the messages to include, e.g. ``role:``."
msgstr "``msgctxt`` predpony správ, ktoré majú obsahovať, napr. ``role:``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mutating_proofs``: required once ``tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` is true. Names the artifact proving each of confirmation, authorization, idempotency, audit and reversal for the mutating variant, separately from the read-only one."
msgstr "``mutating_proofs``: vyžaduje sa raz ``tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` je pravda. Pomenuje artefakt preukazujúci každé potvrdenie, povolenie, nevyváženosť, audit a zvrat pre mutačný variant, oddelene od čítaného."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``name``           the EFFECTIVE docker volume name"
msgstr "``name`` Efektívna docker hlasitosť názov"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``name``: unique mapping id"
msgstr "``name``: jedinečné číslo mapovania"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``networks.internet.dns`` arrives through ``-e @inventories/...`` and is read straight out of ``variables``, which hands back whatever the file contains. While that was a literal address nobody noticed; an expression there reached the daemon as its own source text and docker refused the config with ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."
msgstr "``networks.internet.dns`` prichádza cez ``-e @inventories/...`` a číta sa priamo z ``variables``, ktorý vráti späť čokoľvek súbor obsahuje. Hoci to bola doslovná adresa, nikto si to nevšimol; výraz tam dosiahol démona ako jeho vlastný zdrojový text a Docker odmietol konfig s ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``new_text_or_None`` is ``None`` when nothing changed."
msgstr "``new_text_or_None`` ci ``None`` keď sa nič nezmenilo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``nfs``            NFS opt-in (bool or dict), ``None`` if absent"
msgstr "``nfs`` Opt-in NFS (bool alebo dict), ``None`` ak chýba"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``noqa`` and ``nocheck`` are accepted as synonyms (case-insensitive) by this parser. By repo convention every project rule from ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MUST use ``nocheck:`` because ``# noqa: <code>`` is also parsed by ruff as a flake8 directive and triggers ``invalid-noqa-code`` warnings on every project-specific rule key. ``noqa:`` is reserved for real flake8 / ruff codes (``E402``, ``F401``, …). The ``direct-yaml`` lint enforces the convention by hard-rejecting the ``noqa:`` form."
msgstr "``noqa`` a ``nocheck`` sú akceptované ako synonymá (prípad-necitlivý) týmto parserom. Podľa repo konvencie každé pravidlo projektu ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MUSÍ ``nocheck:`` pretože ``# noqa: <code>`` je tiež parsed by ruff ako vločka8 smernice a spúšťacie mechanizmy ``invalid-noqa-code`` varovania o každom kľúči pre jednotlivé projekty. ``noqa:`` je vyhradený pre skutočné šupky8 / ruff kódy (``E402``, ``F401``, ...). ``direct-yaml`` Lint presadzuje dohovor tým, že tvrdo odmieta ``noqa:`` forma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``offset`` moves that start deliberately: it is how an operator reaches the tail without waiting for anything. It defaults to 0, so every run that does not ask for it deploys the same head and can be compared against the last one. This used to be derived from the sweep number instead, which bought tail coverage at the price of the head -- chunk 0 began wherever the arithmetic pointed, the rows that matter most ran only every few sweeps, and no two runs were comparable."
msgstr "``offset`` pohyby, ktoré začínajú zámerne: je to, ako operátor dosiahne chvost bez čakania na čokoľvek. @ info 0, takže každý beh, ktorý nežiada o to rozmiestňuje rovnakú hlavu a možno ho porovnať s posledným. Toto bolo odvodené od čísla zametania, ktoré namiesto toho kúpilo pokrytie za cenu hlavy -- kus 0 začal všade tam, kde aritmetický špicatý, riadky, ktoré najviac záleží bežal len každých pár kontrol, a žiadne dva behy boli porovnateľné."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc-authenticator`` and ``ldap-authenticator`` are mutually exclusive auth backends (only one may be enabled; see ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` carries only the installer coordinate."
msgstr "``oidc-authenticator`` a ``ldap-authenticator`` sú vzájomne vylučujúce auth backends (iba jeden môže byť povolený; pozri ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` nesie iba súradnicu inštalátora."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc``: baseline admin OIDC round-trip plus the three RBAC scenarios (subscriber/editor/administrator)."
msgstr "``oidc``: základný admin OIDC kruhový výlet plus tri scenáre RBAC (subscriber/editor/administrator)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``openssl_conf_host`` (string): host path for generated openssl.cnf"
msgstr "``openssl_conf_host`` (reťazec): host trasa pre generované openssl.cnf"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``out`` itself lives under the dump dir (both derive from INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), so the walk must skip its own output subtree or copytree recurses into the growing destination until ENAMETOOLONG."
msgstr "``out`` sám žije pod kopačkou (oba pochádzajú z INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), takže chôdza musí preskočiť svoj vlastný výstup podstrom alebo kopírka sa vracia do rastúceho cieľa až do ENAMETOLONG."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the branch lives on."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` vetva žije ďalej."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the run lives in."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` beh žije."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``package.json`` and ``playwright.config.js`` are provided centrally by this role:"
msgstr "``package.json`` a ``playwright.config.js`` sú centrálne poskytované touto úlohou:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``package_name`` (string) Name of the Python package to install (e.g., ``dockreap``, ``backup-docker-to-local``)."
msgstr "``package_name`` (reťazec) Názov balíka Python na inštaláciu (napr. ``dockreap``, ``backup-docker-to-local``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``password`` (should come from vault/credentials)"
msgstr "``password`` (by mali pochádzať z trezoru/dôvery)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``path``           the legacy ``path:`` field, ``''`` if absent"
msgstr "``path`` odkaz ``path:`` pole, ``''`` ak chýba"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``phpunit/phpunit`` declares ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` as platform requirements and Composer refuses to resolve the vendor tree without them, so they are part of the toolchain rather than of the suite consuming it. A distro ships them as packages separate from the interpreter, which is why a present ``php`` binary does not imply they are there."
msgstr "``phpunit/phpunit`` vyhlásenie ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` ako požiadavky platformy a Skladateľ odmieta vyriešiť predajcu strom bez nich, takže sú súčasťou nástrojového reťazca, a nie apartmánu spotrebuje. Distro ich posiela ako balíky oddelené od tlmočníka, a preto je prítomný ``php`` binárne neznamená, že sú tam."

# translation-refused: libretranslate truncated
# nocheck: url
# translation-rejected: ``playwright.spec.js``
# ``guest``/``biber``/``administrator`` osobnosti. EÚ ``biber`` /
