# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``playwright.version`` in ``meta/services.yml`` is the single source of truth for the default Playwright version; the central ``templates/package.json.j2`` pins it via the ``image_version`` filter."
msgstr "``playwright.version`` on ``meta/services.yml`` je jediným zdrojom pravdy pre predvolenú verziu Playwright; centrálne ``templates/package.json.j2`` kolíky cez ``image_version`` filter."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``plg_system_keycloak`` is built imperatively inside the Joomla container and speaks OIDC against Keycloak. Its enablement derives directly from the ``sso`` service flag, and its OIDC runtime contract (issuer, client id/secret, redirect/end-session URLs, fallback toggle, and RBAC group paths) lives under the addon’s ``config:`` block, which ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` plugin environment."
msgstr "``plg_system_keycloak`` je postavený nevyhnutne vnútri Joomla kontajner a hovorí OIDC proti KeycloakJej možnosť pochádza priamo z ``sso`` servisná vlajka a jej prevádzková zmluva OIDC (Emitent, klient id/secret, presmerovanie/koncové URL URL, prepnutie a RBAC skupinové cesty) život pod sudomi ``config:`` blok, ktorý ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` prostredie modulu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``poll: 0`` makes a task fire and forget, so its own ``changed_when`` and ``failed_when`` never see an outcome. The outcome only exists once the job is collected with ``async_status``, and collecting it is where the verdict has to be made -- for a whole batch at once, so one run reports every broken job rather than the first."
msgstr "``poll: 0`` robí úlohu oheň a zabudnúť, takže jeho vlastné ``changed_when`` a ``failed_when`` Nikdy nevidieť výsledok. Výsledok existuje len vtedy, keď sa práca získa ``async_status``, a zbieranie je miesto, kde sa musí urobiť verdikt -- pre celú dávku naraz, takže jeden beh hlási každú zlomenú prácu skôr ako prvý."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ports.onion`` is a category-keyed map of booleans alongside ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: it names which of a service's already-declared ports should answer on the node onion, and nothing else. The port number comes from ``ports.local`` when that category is declared there and from ``ports.public`` otherwise, which is the precedence ``container_ports`` publishes by, so the forward always targets the port the service is actually reachable on."
msgstr "``ports.onion`` je mapa booleanov na kľúč vedľa ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: to názvy, ktoré služby už deklarované prístavy by mali odpovedať na uzol cibule, a nič iné. Číslo prístavu pochádza z ``ports.local`` ak je táto kategória deklarovaná tam a z ``ports.public`` inak, čo je prednosť ``container_ports`` Publikuje, takže dopredu vždy ciele prístavu služba je skutočne dosiahnuteľný na."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``priority`` IS the retrigger: it names what failed. ``offset`` is recomputed rather than carried, but from the carried value up: the source run got a stretch behind its own offset green before its budget ran out, so the regular line resumes behind that stretch (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) instead of repeating it, and never falls back behind where that run started. Everything else is carried verbatim, including ``whitelist``, so a retrigger of a scoped run stays inside that scope instead of quietly widening to the whole repository."
msgstr "``priority`` JE retrigger: to, čo zlyhalo. ``offset`` je recomputovaný skôr ako prenášaný, ale z prevedenej hodnoty nahor: zdroj beh dostal úsek za svojou vlastnou ofset green pred vyčerpaním rozpočtu, takže pravidelná linka pokračuje za týmto úsekom (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) namiesto toho, aby som to opakoval, a nikdy nezaostane tam, kde to začalo. Všetko ostatné sa nesie doslovne, vrátane ``whitelist``, takže retiger scaped spustiť zostane vo vnútri tohto rozsahu namiesto ticho rozšíriť do celého úložiska."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: for ``onion_sso``, the app whose"
msgstr "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: pre ``onion_sso``, aplikácia, ktorej"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``provides`` matching runs in both directions, so a provider (e.g. openldap ``provides: ldap``) is picked up even when the consuming flag uses a ``groups[...]`` form the ``group_names`` regex cannot read."
msgstr "``provides`` zodpovedajúce beží v oboch smeroch, takže poskytovateľ (napr. openldap ``provides: ldap``) je vyzdvihnutá aj keď konzumná vlajka používa ``groups[...]`` form ``group_names`` regex nevie čítať."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_aliases``: aliases the beacon exposes for harvesting; falls back"
msgstr "``proxy_aliases``: prezývky maják vystavuje na zber; spadne"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_pass`` directive; swarm prepends a ``set`` line (request-time DNS)."
msgstr "``proxy_pass`` smernica; roj pripravuje ``set`` čiara (čas žiadosti DNS)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_resolvable``: beacon flag - the harvested aliases get attached to"
msgstr "``proxy_resolvable``: vlajka majáka - zozbierané prezývky sa pripoja k"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``quay.io/centos/centos:latest`` becomes ``centos:latest``; a two-segment image such as ``debian:13`` is returned unchanged."
msgstr "``quay.io/centos/centos:latest`` sa stáva ``centos:latest``; dvojsegmentový obraz ako ``debian:13`` sa vráti v nezmenenej podobe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``reason``:          why a non-deployable classification cannot serve."
msgstr "``reason``: prečo nezamestnateľná klasifikácia nemôže slúžiť."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``relay`` and ``media`` are UDP. ``stun_turn`` and its TLS variant do speak TCP, but the allocation they hand out is a UDP relay address the onion client can never receive on, so forwarding the signalling port buys nothing."
msgstr "``relay`` a ``media`` sú UDP. ``stun_turn`` a jeho TLS variant hovoria TCP, ale prideľovanie, ktoré rozdávajú, je UDP relé adresu klienta cibuľa nemôže nikdy prijímať, takže zasielanie návestného portu nenakupuje nič."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``repo`` carries the repository the names come from, defined inline on the entry that needs it: a full definition (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) rendered as a yum repo, ``bootstrap_package`` for a repo shipped as a package such as ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` to switch on a repo the distro already ships, ``pacman_section`` to uncomment a section of ``pacman.conf`` such as ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` for a community repository, or ``managed_externally`` when the role sets it up itself."
msgstr "``repo`` obsahuje úložisko, z ktorého pochádzajú názvy definované v riadku, ktorý ich potrebuje: úplná definícia (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) prevedený ako mňam repo, ``bootstrap_package`` pre repo expedovanie ako balík, ako napríklad ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` na zapnutie repo distro už lode, ``pacman_section`` odpojiť časť ``pacman.conf`` ako napríklad ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` pre úložisko Spoločenstva alebo ``managed_externally`` keď sa úloha sama vytvorí."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``repos`` or ``upstreams``."
msgstr "``repos`` alebo ``upstreams``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed)"
msgstr "``required`` (vždy nainštalovaný)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed, vendored)"
msgstr "``required`` (vždy nainštalovaný, predáva)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``requirepass`` for the ``default`` (admin) user, sourced from the ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` credential."
msgstr "``requirepass`` pre ``default`` (admin) používateľ, ktorý pochádza z ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` Poverený."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``retries`` counts CONSECUTIVE failures, and a request that leaves the container is load balanced across the service VIP. With N replicas and one of them alive, a round robin never produces more than N-1 failures in a row, so a streak based check is arithmetically blind to losing all but one backend. Chaining ``samples`` requests into a single probe makes one probe cover the whole pool instead."
msgstr "``retries`` počíta konzistentné poruchy a požiadavka, ktorá opúšťa kontajner, je vyvážená v celom servisnom VIP. S N replikami a jednou z nich živou, okrúhla Robin nikdy nevyprodukuje viac ako N-1 poruchy v rade, takže pruh založený na kontrole je aritmeticky slepý stratiť všetky okrem jedného backendu. Reťazce ``samples`` požiadavky do jednej sondy namiesto toho pokryjú celý bazén."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``role`` may be a role name (relative to ``roles/``) or an absolute path to a role directory. Pass ``role_name`` explicitly when ``role`` is an arbitrary path whose basename is not the canonical role name."
msgstr "``role`` môže byť názov úlohy (vo vzťahu k ``roles/``) alebo absolútna cesta do adresára úloh. Pass ``role_name`` výslovne keď ``role`` je svojvoľná cesta, ktorej základné meno nie je kanonické meno role."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` declares ``status_codes`` keyed like ``domains.canonical``; it is the single source of truth for every prober."
msgstr "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` vyhlásenie ``status_codes`` keyed like ``domains.canonical``; je to jediný zdroj pravdy pre každý sonder."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Follow `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ and `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ while creating them."
msgstr "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Nasledujte `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ a `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ pri ich vytváraní."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` is the SPOT for both the repository and the version of every GitHub-release lint tool. Each entry carries the ``repository`` / ``ref`` pair that ``utils.update.repository`` already scans, so the existing ``update-repository-refs`` CI job bumps the pins to the latest semver tag and opens a PR -- the same machinery that keeps ``roles/pkgmgr`` current."
msgstr "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` je SPOT pre úložisko aj verziu každého nástroja GitHub-release Lint. Každý záznam nesie ``repository`` / ``ref`` pár, ktorý ``utils.update.repository`` už skenuje, takže existujúce ``update-repository-refs`` Práca CI narazí na kolíky na najnovšiu značku Semver a otvorí PR -- rovnaké stroje, ktoré udržujú ``roles/pkgmgr`` prúd."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js`` (copied as-is)"
msgstr "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js`` (skopírované ako)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2`` (rendered per-deploy; pins ``@playwright/test`` from ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``)"
msgstr "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2`` (vyrobené na jedno použitie; kolíky ``@playwright/test`` od ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles_with_service('mcp', direction='server')`` entries."
msgstr "``roles_with_service('mcp', direction='server')`` položky."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``run_after``  — project-specific role-load-order list."
msgstr "``run_after``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``run_after`` is deliberately NOT read: it is a deploy-ordering hint, not a runtime dependency. The wider cosmos (federation peers, external bridged networks) cannot be derived from metadata and is left for the author to add."
msgstr "``run_after`` je zámerne NIE čítať: je to nasadenie-objednávka, nie závislosť. Širší vesmír (federácie, externé premostené siete) nemožno odvodiť z metadát a je ponechaný na autora pridať."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` validates the generated packaging metadata with each ecosystem's native parser. This installer provisions those parsers wherever the platform's package manager can: on Debian (apt) the lint container gets ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) and ``rpmlint``; on Arch (pacman) a dev host gets ``namcap``."
msgstr "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` Validuje vytvorené obalové metaúdaje s pôvodným parserom každého ekosystému. Tento inštalátor poskytuje tie parsery, kde správca balíkov platformy môže: na Debiane (apt) kontajner na linty dostane ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) a ``rpmlint``; na oblúku (pacman) zbožný hostiteľ dostane ``namcap``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``semantic_name``  the YAML key from ``meta/volumes.yml``"
msgstr "``semantic_name`` kľúč YAML od ``meta/volumes.yml``"

